WEBVTT

00:07.810 --> 00:09.980
<i>I was a king.</i>

00:14.030 --> 00:15.310
<i>The strongest king.</i>

00:32.140 --> 00:38.890
<i>And as king, I took countless lives,
committing countless sins.</i>

00:41.480 --> 00:43.100
<i>And yet, I now find myself...</i>

00:53.190 --> 00:56.360
We've got another quest, Arthur.

00:57.320 --> 01:00.170
Okay. Let's go, Jasmine.

01:03.420 --> 01:06.710
<i>Granted a second life.</i>

02:40.280 --> 02:45.010
#1 The King Begins Adventuring.

02:46.460 --> 02:47.730
Let's go over the details.

02:48.330 --> 02:52.000
Contact with a village near the
Beast Glades has been lost.

02:52.000 --> 02:54.020
We've been asked to investigate.

02:54.020 --> 02:55.710
And our priorities?

02:55.710 --> 02:57.010
Survival first.

02:57.530 --> 03:00.030
If we find an aggressive beast?

03:00.270 --> 03:02.280
The quest does not include slaying,

03:02.280 --> 03:04.530
so there no need to do so.

03:04.530 --> 03:05.690
Very good.

03:06.540 --> 03:08.120
<i>What are you gonna do, Sylvie?</i>

03:08.430 --> 03:10.650
<i>I'll be training nearby.</i>

03:10.650 --> 03:12.850
<i>Got it. I'll let you know when we're done.</i>

03:12.850 --> 03:14.990
<i>Good luck, Arthur!</i>

03:25.180 --> 03:27.680
Notice anything, Note?

03:28.260 --> 03:33.310
There are tracks heading into the village,
but not many heading away from it.

03:33.950 --> 03:35.350
What do we do first?

03:35.350 --> 03:37.320
Gather intelligence.

03:37.710 --> 03:38.620
Correct.

03:50.290 --> 03:51.990
No signs of any people.

03:52.900 --> 03:54.390
Did a beast attack them?

03:54.790 --> 03:57.300
That'd make the lack of signs 
of a struggle very strange.

04:00.520 --> 04:01.350
Note.

04:02.490 --> 04:03.840
What is that?

04:04.310 --> 04:05.290
Let's find out.

04:08.120 --> 04:09.460
Crystals?

04:10.260 --> 04:11.830
But why would they be out here?

04:20.170 --> 04:21.130
Jasmine...

04:28.950 --> 04:30.720
Can you tell us what happened?

04:30.720 --> 04:35.370
I dunno. I was in the forest,
 gathering medicinal herbs...

04:35.770 --> 04:37.310
And when I got back...

04:41.930 --> 04:43.690
A beast did this.

04:43.690 --> 04:45.850
Yeah. But...

05:00.460 --> 05:02.450
No! No!

05:03.650 --> 05:04.570
Why?!

05:05.730 --> 05:06.570
We can't.

05:09.690 --> 05:12.230
No! Mommy—

05:16.690 --> 05:17.580
We're running.

05:33.010 --> 05:37.960
The tri-kingdom alliance between 
humans, elves, and dwarves:

05:37.960 --> 05:41.360
a less than ideal arrangement, 
from where we stand.

05:41.800 --> 05:44.230
All events have a flow to them.

05:44.550 --> 05:47.740
Sometimes, going with that 
flow can be quite pleasant.

05:51.010 --> 05:52.990
The Beast Glade?

05:53.690 --> 05:57.970
Those who will bear the future of 
this continent on their backs gather,

05:57.970 --> 05:59.750
in order to hone themselves.

06:01.310 --> 06:02.810
The future...

06:03.960 --> 06:07.310
Something we must prevent at all costs.

06:08.520 --> 06:11.070
I had thought this task 
would be tiresome,

06:11.070 --> 06:13.260
but it's not without its charms.

06:16.650 --> 06:17.690
What was it?

06:17.690 --> 06:22.270
An Arachne: one of the top five beasts 
I never want to have to fight.

06:22.680 --> 06:24.000
Have you fought Arachne before?

06:24.000 --> 06:26.870
Five times. Only managed to kill one.

06:27.550 --> 06:29.810
It took the entire lineup 
of the Twinhorns.

06:31.740 --> 06:35.850
Reynolds and Alice, your 
parents, were there, too.

06:37.250 --> 06:40.540
Alice in particular was 
critical to winning.

06:40.860 --> 06:42.580
Because of her Emitter powers?

06:42.580 --> 06:43.540
Exactly.

06:44.090 --> 06:47.060
An Arachne's curse can only 
be broken by an Emitter,

06:47.510 --> 06:50.660
or by killing the Arachne.

06:51.550 --> 06:55.670
But Arachne have high resistance to magic.
Most spells have limited effect.

06:56.170 --> 06:59.290
Plus, their carapace is tough enough 
that swords bounce off it.

06:59.290 --> 07:01.810
Then we don't have the 
means to take it down.

07:01.810 --> 07:06.060
Yeah. But Arachne hate daylight.

07:06.460 --> 07:09.320
They normally stay deep inside dungeons.

07:10.030 --> 07:13.660
More importantly, Note... or, Arthur.

07:14.020 --> 07:18.080
I've taught you everything I know
about being an adventurer.

07:19.220 --> 07:21.800
Not just how to fight 
with swords and sorcery.

07:23.450 --> 07:27.980
I've taught you the things 
you need to survive.

07:29.380 --> 07:33.430
So, in light of that, I ask you: 
what should we do right now?

07:37.070 --> 07:37.990
Let's head back.

07:38.590 --> 07:42.850
We'll inform the Guild and save the 
village once we're fully prepared.

07:49.970 --> 07:50.490
Arthur!

07:53.500 --> 07:54.510
Jasmine!

07:54.990 --> 07:56.240
Get away, Arthur!

07:56.730 --> 07:58.740
Even if you're the only one—

08:40.270 --> 08:42.100
<i>Now you've done it.</i>

08:58.510 --> 09:02.180
<i>I was once a king.</i>

09:05.580 --> 09:09.060
<i>A king who was known as the strongest.</i>

09:17.050 --> 09:19.200
<i>A single swing of my blade...</i>

09:31.500 --> 09:34.030
<i>...was all it took to win my battles.</i>

09:47.640 --> 09:49.570
Swords won't be enough.

10:00.750 --> 10:03.040
<i>Let's try blade and flame.</i>

10:08.830 --> 10:10.270
This seems to be getting through.

10:18.120 --> 10:19.050
Was that enough?

10:23.930 --> 10:25.270
I see.

10:25.580 --> 10:28.540
Jasmine did mention it 
had magic resistance.

10:45.290 --> 10:46.540
It's pointless.

11:17.100 --> 11:20.070
Have you ever had magic 
cast on your insides?

11:28.390 --> 11:30.110
I want Jasmine back!

11:48.580 --> 11:49.560
Jasmine.

11:57.030 --> 11:59.110
<i>You really don't know when you're beat.</i>

12:01.710 --> 12:04.240
<i>There is one thing I'm grateful for...</i>

12:05.500 --> 12:09.370
<i>You've helped me remember 
how I used to wield a sword.</i>

12:26.620 --> 12:28.670
<i>The strain is still too much.</i>

12:31.170 --> 12:37.770
<i>My old way of fighting, and the new power 
I've gained with this world's magic...</i>

12:38.170 --> 12:40.330
<i>I'm a long way from what I'm aiming for.</i>

12:42.460 --> 12:44.200
<i>I'll need to train more.</i>

12:45.300 --> 12:50.890
<i>Arthur!</i>

12:53.770 --> 12:58.790
<i>You okay? Did something happen?
You felt really angry for a second.</i>

12:59.590 --> 13:02.990
<i>Yeah, but it's fine now.
 I took care of it.</i>

13:03.780 --> 13:05.060
<i>You sure?</i>

13:05.060 --> 13:06.300
<i>Yeah, I'm sure.</i>

13:06.520 --> 13:09.700
<i>Okay, then. Well, good luck.</i>

13:09.700 --> 13:11.180
<i>With what?</i>

13:11.180 --> 13:12.110
<i>That.</i>

13:16.330 --> 13:19.650
Jasmine... good to see 
that the curse is broken!

13:20.190 --> 13:22.220
I could beat you easily right now, y'know.

13:23.110 --> 13:24.620
Don't joke like that!

13:25.740 --> 13:27.520
You're not laughing...

13:27.520 --> 13:29.320
Is that seriously all you have to say?

13:32.670 --> 13:33.740
I'm sorry.

13:34.110 --> 13:35.560
What are you apologizing for?

13:36.350 --> 13:40.340
The fact that I fought that thing, 
ignoring your instructions.

13:41.580 --> 13:43.660
I let my emotions get carried away.

13:44.700 --> 13:46.200
As long as you understand.

13:47.950 --> 13:50.350
You really did beat it by yourself, huh?

13:50.830 --> 13:52.220
That's all I did.

13:52.580 --> 13:55.480
This might be power that I need, 
but it's not the power I want.

13:56.280 --> 13:58.450
And power do you want?

13:59.260 --> 14:00.860
The power to protect.

14:01.580 --> 14:07.910
My weakness separated me 
from Dad, Mom, and Eleanor.

14:08.940 --> 14:13.180
If I had been stronger, I could've 
protected the people I care about.

14:15.410 --> 14:16.740
I'm sorry.

14:16.740 --> 14:18.460
It's not your fault.

14:18.940 --> 14:21.460
And there's no redoing the past.

14:24.610 --> 14:28.360
I just have to live in a way that 
will leave me with no regrets.

14:30.590 --> 14:34.050
All that said, if something 
happened to you,

14:34.050 --> 14:35.750
Alice and the others would be devastated.

14:36.180 --> 14:38.360
Don't take risks on my behalf.

14:38.360 --> 14:39.460
I can't do that.

14:40.620 --> 14:44.110
I care about you too, Jasmine.

14:48.180 --> 14:52.130
Y-You had better not think 
I'll forgive you for that.

14:52.130 --> 14:54.090
That wasn't my intention.

14:55.400 --> 14:57.390
The only thing you 
get better at is talking.

14:57.390 --> 14:59.580
I mean it!

15:03.960 --> 15:05.830
Thank you for saving me.

15:06.310 --> 15:07.630
Don't mention it.

15:10.870 --> 15:14.430
Oh, we should collect 
the Arachne's mana core.

15:39.070 --> 15:41.160
You fought an Arachne?!

15:41.630 --> 15:43.330
I'm amazed you made it back alive.

15:43.330 --> 15:44.900
I just got lucky.

15:45.410 --> 15:46.710
Hey, Note.

15:47.630 --> 15:50.170
Are you serious about 
this Arachne business?

15:50.400 --> 15:52.930
Lucas, again with this?

15:52.930 --> 15:57.680
It's only natural to have doubts. 
Arachne never come to the surface.

15:58.100 --> 16:00.700
You're not making it up, are you?

16:00.700 --> 16:02.810
What would it take for you to believe me?

16:03.140 --> 16:05.620
Show me the Arachne's mana core.

16:10.310 --> 16:12.890
Unfortunately, we weren't 
able to collect it.

16:14.090 --> 16:16.570
Well, that doesn't make your 
story any less suspicious!

16:16.810 --> 16:20.790
Maybe you actually ran 
into a giant spider?

16:24.600 --> 16:26.470
How's this for evidence?

16:27.230 --> 16:28.850
A Cursing Eye of Petrification?

16:30.390 --> 16:31.580
It's the real deal.

16:32.170 --> 16:33.460
No way...

16:33.460 --> 16:35.590
I've never seen one before.

16:36.830 --> 16:37.820
Damn, that's hard.

16:37.820 --> 16:39.860
How in the hell did you cut this thing?

16:40.190 --> 16:41.730
Well, Lucas?

16:42.870 --> 16:45.350
Looks like you're not lying!

16:45.690 --> 16:50.630
But a mana beast like this 
would be no match for me.

16:51.670 --> 16:55.530
I'll be sure to call on you for 
help next time, Lucas Wykes.

16:57.220 --> 16:58.370
Let's go!

16:59.070 --> 17:01.410
He never changes.

17:02.050 --> 17:03.620
Sure doesn't.

17:04.100 --> 17:06.370
Note, we should get going.

17:06.730 --> 17:07.990
Are you going on a trip?

17:07.990 --> 17:09.220
Just a trip home.

17:13.950 --> 17:15.380
I'm back!

17:15.380 --> 17:17.640
Arthur!

17:17.920 --> 17:21.640
I'd be thrilled to hear about the 
epic adventure you got up to,

17:21.930 --> 17:23.420
as the family's hero.

17:25.260 --> 17:27.570
You beat an Arachne?!

17:28.150 --> 17:30.070
Unbelievable...

17:28.150 --> 17:30.650
That's amazing, Arthur!

17:30.920 --> 17:35.270
We had such a hard time 
against them! Right, Jasmine?

17:35.270 --> 17:38.320
Yeah. We were nearly 
wiped out four times.

17:38.320 --> 17:40.340
That's amazing, Arthur!

17:40.910 --> 17:42.660
How in the world did you manage that?

17:42.910 --> 17:46.920
Well, it was so hard, I had to 
focus my attacks on a single spot.

17:47.360 --> 17:50.350
And I figured magic would work if
I could cast it on its insides.

17:52.040 --> 17:53.920
You all need to kneel.

17:56.410 --> 17:59.810
I seem to remember a promise about 
not doing anything dangerous.

17:59.810 --> 18:01.390
A promise <i>you</i> made, didn't you?!

18:01.390 --> 18:05.810
I know, but... that's kind of 
impossible for an adventurer.

18:05.810 --> 18:08.270
A promise is a promise!

18:08.270 --> 18:09.400
I'm sorry!

18:09.400 --> 18:13.700
Jasmine! You were with him! 
How could you let this happen?!

18:13.700 --> 18:14.940
I'm sorry.

18:14.940 --> 18:20.190
An Arachne is in the top five beasts 
that you should run from on sight!

18:20.190 --> 18:21.540
I'm sorry.

18:21.540 --> 18:24.850
It's not Jasmine's fault! 
I was the one who—

18:24.850 --> 18:26.980
I'm talking to her right now!

18:26.980 --> 18:28.390
I'm sorry.

18:28.390 --> 18:29.770
I'm sorry.

18:30.210 --> 18:33.220
I let you go because you insisted, Arthur.

18:33.530 --> 18:36.710
And Jasmine said she'd teach you
 everything you need to know.

18:36.710 --> 18:39.800
That's the only reason I allowed 
you to become an adventurer!

18:40.600 --> 18:42.220
And now?!

18:42.720 --> 18:46.870
I hear about you fighting something 
as dangerous as an Arachne!

18:46.870 --> 18:51.450
And you somehow managed to beat it?!

18:52.470 --> 18:54.730
There, there.

18:56.250 --> 19:01.340
Arthur. Next time, make sure to 
do as Jasmine says. Understood?

19:03.220 --> 19:04.060
Right.

19:04.520 --> 19:07.020
Jasmine, about the Arachne...

19:07.020 --> 19:09.500
I already told the Guild to look into it.

19:09.850 --> 19:13.700
Good job. I'll warn Helen and 
the others to be careful.

19:15.000 --> 19:18.150
Come on, Mom, cheer up.

19:19.240 --> 19:22.760
What Arthur did was dangerous, but 
what he accomplished was remarkable.

19:23.340 --> 19:29.100
I don't mean beating the Arachne.
I mean making it back to us safely.

19:29.100 --> 19:31.270
Yes, you're right.

19:32.040 --> 19:35.890
Arthur... just don't 
make me worry too much.

19:35.890 --> 19:37.670
I understand, Mom.

19:40.920 --> 19:42.420
I got yelled at.

19:43.610 --> 19:46.200
Alice has always been 
the scariest of us all.

19:46.540 --> 19:48.790
I think I understand why.

19:49.060 --> 19:51.540
Try not to upset her next time.

19:52.330 --> 19:53.370
You're right.

20:02.290 --> 20:03.640
No magic.

20:05.610 --> 20:06.510
Right.

20:12.520 --> 20:14.900
<i>What I lacked in my past life...</i>

20:18.020 --> 20:20.860
<i>...is the thing I've promised 
to defend in this life.</i>

20:24.090 --> 20:27.460
<i>And to do that, I need more power.</i>

20:28.950 --> 20:32.470
<i>The power to defend the 
people I care about.</i>

20:39.550 --> 20:41.460
Thank you for the match.

20:49.100 --> 20:50.450
<i>What's wrong?</i>

20:51.400 --> 20:53.480
<i>I just remembering something.</i>

20:57.930 --> 21:00.190
<i>She was like a gale wind.</i>

21:01.550 --> 21:05.300
<i>I wonder what Tessia's up to.</i>

21:06.260 --> 21:12.270
Why, why, why, oh why, did 
nobody warn me about this?!

21:13.050 --> 21:16.100
Someone should have, right?!
